 fragment='''<section class="card" id="components"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">OFF-THE-SHELF COMPONENTS · FOUR-MOTOR RESEARCH RIG</p><h2>What to rent, buy and quote.</h2></div><div class="links"><a href="components/bom.csv" download>Component CSV ↓</a><a href="components/quotation-brief.txt" download>Quotation brief ↓</a></div></div><p>Start with XAS 88 rental, matched air treatment and four loaded LZB46 motors. Use four wide slots as the first delivery configuration. This list covers the equipment needed to test the source assumption; it does not establish that the motors deliver the CFD’s 0.96°C air.</p><div class="plant-flow" aria-label="System flow"><span>Compressor<br><b>XAS 88 candidate</b></span><i>→</i><span>Aftercooler / separator<br><b>DD + PD → FD → QD / dust</b></span><i>→</i><span>Warm valve / manifold<br><b>4 regulated branches</b></span><i>→</i><span>4 loaded motors<br><b>4 × 840 W shaft work</b></span><i>→</i><span>Short insulated hoses<br><b>4 × 280 × 40 mm slots</b></span></div><p class="note">Each shaft connects to a commercial external load station. Reject the load’s heat outside the cold stream and target. The pressure regulator controls supply; it does not replace shaft-work extraction. No cold-output pressure tank is selected.</p><div class="banner warn"><strong>Main open fit:</strong> stock motor exhaust → short, large cold branch → printed 100 mm spigot. Exact motor ports, adapters, load coupling and the installed source temperature need verification. Manufacturer model identification is separate from a sized, fitted quotation. Prices and local stock are unverified.</div><div class="plant-calculator"><div><h3>Supply and hose sizing</h3><p class="note">Conditional calculations for four motors at nominal load. These controls never change saved CFD fields.</p><label>Compressor<select id="plantCompressor"></select></label><label>Delivered FAD factor <output id="plantFactorValue"></output><input id="plantFactor" type="range" min="0.6" max="1" step="0.01" value="1"></label><p class="note">Assumed capacity retention after derating / air losses. Use the supplier’s actual value.</p><label>Total treatment / valve / meter loss (bar)<input id="plantTreatment" type="number" min="0" max="2" step="0.05" value="0.3"></label><label>Main hose length (m)<input id="plantMainLength" type="number" min="0" max="50" step="1" value="10"></label><label>Main clear ID (mm)<select id="plantMainID"><option>25</option><option>32</option><option selected>38</option></select></label><label>Each cold hose length (m)<input id="plantColdLength" type="number" min="0" max="10" step="0.25" value="1"></label><label>Each cold hose clear ID (mm)<select id="plantColdID"><option>40</option><option selected>50</option><option>63</option><option>100</option></select></label><label>Assumed exhaust neck bore (mm)<select id="plantNeck"><option selected>16</option><option>20</option><option>25</option><option>32</option></select></label><p class="note">16 mm is a recommended hose-size proxy, not a measured port. Other values are sensitivity inputs, not motor modifications.</p><label>Optional warm receiver (L)<select id="plantTank"><option value="0">None</option><option>100</option><option>250</option><option>500</option></select></label></div><div><div id="plantMetrics" class="plant-metrics" aria-live="polite"></div><p id="plantAssessment" class="banner"></p><p id="plantLosses" class="note"></p><p id="plantThermal" class="note"></p><p id="plantStorage" class="note"></p><details><summary>Calculation assumptions</summary><p class="note">Darcy–Weisbach estimates use the existing panel/model.js implementation, ideal-gas density, 40°C warm air, atmospheric cold air, 4 × 19.4 g/s and equal branches. Warm branch: 2 m / 19 mm ID. Main and branch fitting K=2; neck: 50 mm long with K=1 assumed. The neck bore and K need a drawing/test. The 1–2 kPa exhaust flag is the design-document screen, not a manufacturer limit. Warm losses exclude unmeasured internal motor inlet restrictions and regulator droop.</p><p class="note">Cold hose-only heat leak assumes a 3 mm polymer wall (k=0.2), 19 mm insulation (k=0.035), external h=8 W/(m²·K), 30°C surroundings and −3.04°C entering air from the conditional first law. It excludes motor/body heat, joints, solar heat and startup. No moisture transport is calculated. Receiver storage uses selected source pressure → calculated running-supply floor, 40°C and isothermal inventory; this is an optimistic storage screen.</p></details><h3>Listed compressor comparison</h3><div class="table"><table class="plant-compressors"><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>bar g</th><th>FAD m³/min</th><th>After factor</th><th>Flow screen</th></tr></thead><tbody id="plantCompressorRows"></tbody></table></div><p class="note">Same four-motor requirement. 15% planning allowance is an assumption. Higher source pressure does not guarantee more FAD; keep the actual pressure/FAD pair.</p></div></div><div class="catalogue-controls"><label>Component stage<select id="componentStage"><option value="all">All items</option>'''+''.join(f'<option>{h(s)}</option>' for s in dict.fromkeys(r['stage'] for r in rows))+'''</select></label><label>Find component<input id="componentSearch" type="search" placeholder="Motor, filter, hose, meter…"></label><p id="componentCount" role="status"></p></div><div class="table"><table class="component-table"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Quantity</th><th>Component / purpose / evidence</th><th>Acquire</th><th>Readiness</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+table+'''</tbody></table></div><div class="two procurement-next"><div><h3>First acquisition</h3><p>Rent one complete motor/load test station with the same air treatment. Measure power, mass flow, inlet/exhaust temperature and backpressure. Confirm a usable source point before scaling the purchase to four motors and four loads. Retain the full-system compressor quote for the later test.</p></div><div><h3>Buffer choice</h3><p>No cold buffer tank initially. A small cold plenum can balance flow, but adds volume, wall heat and startup delay. A warm receiver is optional for compressor response. It cannot fix inadequate average compressor flow over repeated sprays.</p></div></div><p class="note">The CFD slider selects delivery experiments. Reducing motor inlet flow changes its operating point. To reproduce lower-flow CFD at the same temperature, qualify a stock exhaust diversion / metering arrangement and measure the delivered boundary; it is not part of the present fitted assembly.</p><div class="links"><a href="components/bom.json">Specs, sources and unresolved items</a><a href="../cad/outlet-280x40-print-mm.stl" download>Starting slot STL</a><a href="../../pass-by-study/cad/hose-fit-coupon-OD100-mm.stl" download>100 mm hose fit coupon</a><a href="#source-temperature">Conditional source calculation</a><a href="#nozzle-catalogue">All nozzle CAD / CFD</a></div><p class="note">Manufacturer pages checked 23 Oct 2026. Numerical sizing is not Lean-verified. No order, supplier enquiry or hardware qualification has been made.</p></section>'''
